## Context

The author targets a non-causal comparative paper on traceable JETP finance,
lifecycle states, denominators and coverage across four countries. The old figure
mixes political-pledge denominators with historical commitment denominators and
cannot answer this question.

Plan: `conception/jetp-observatory-and-papers-plan.md`. Parent tracker: 0725.

## First test

First figure acceptance check: every JETP and historical mark uses the same defined transition and clock, with cohort size and missingness traceable to 0730. A pledge-normalised flow or partnership-age proxy must fail this check. A null or mixed difference must render and remain reportable.

## Actions

Rewrite conception/jetp-papier-court-mesure.md around 0730/0823 and produce the
LaTeX manuscript in deliverables/jetp-mesure via 0711. Replace the old figure
with the supported comparative figure. Explain lifecycle definitions, coverage
and limits. Do not make instrument substitution or acceleration a claim.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Question, methods and central figure implement the frozen non-causal measurement protocol
- [ ] Manuscript reports supported descriptive findings including null/mixed outcomes
- [ ] Preparation bottlenecks distinguished from execution among approved projects
- [ ] Old disbursement-only and predetermined-mechanism claims reconciled
- [ ] Reproducible LaTeX manuscript with evidence-linked tables and limitations, ready for review

## Validation

Apply the repository gates for the actual diff. Code work starts with the failing
fixture above; prose/data work records the documentary acceptance check. Preserve
source evidence and report limits rather than manufacturing a successful result.

